Project: Real Estate ML System
Authors: Walaa Magdy and Abdelrahman Sayed
Note: Walaa Magdy is the owner and the author of this project (and she's much nice and a little cold 🥶)


PREFECT STARTUP (run 5 minutes before scheduled time)

Open two terminals and run one command in each.

Terminal 1 (run first):
cd "/Users/abdelrahmansayed/Real estate Project" && poetry run prefect server start

Terminal 2 (run 5 seconds after Terminal 1):
cd "/Users/abdelrahmansayed/Real estate Project" && poetry run prefect worker start --pool "data-pipeline-pool"


PROJECT FILES

engine.py          Playwright scraper
normalize.py       Field mapping
schema.py          Pydantic validation (Gate 1)
rules.py           Business rules (Gate 2)
ingest.py          Orchestrates normalize, dedupe, validate, MongoDB
transform.py       MongoDB to PostgreSQL
cleaning.py        Cleans PostgreSQL data into clean_properties table
main.py            Runs everything


SYSTEM FLOW

Scraper
normalize
checksum generation
deduplication check
Gate 1 - schema validation
Gate 2 - business rules
MongoDB storage
Transform to PostgreSQL
Clean to clean_properties


PIPELINE COMPONENTS

normalize.py         Maps raw scraped fields into standard schema
checksum.py          Detects whether listing is NEW, DUPLICATE, or UPDATED
schema.py            Validates and converts raw data types into structured format
rules.py             Applies business logic validation rules
property_logger.py   Handles logging of approved and rejected listings
ingest.py            Main orchestrator that runs the full pipeline


PROCESSING STEPS

1. Raw data collected by scraper
2. Data normalized into standard format
3. Checksum generated using key fields
4. System checks listing status:
   - DUPLICATE: skip and store in duplicate collection
   - NEW or UPDATED: continue processing
5. Gate 1 validation:
   - Converts strings to proper types
   - Rejects invalid formats
6. Gate 2 validation:
   - Ensures business logic is correct
   - Examples: price > 0, area > 0, valid links
7. Final storage decision:
   - Approved: stored in raw_listings
   - Rejected: stored in rejected_listings


MONGODB COLLECTIONS

raw_listings          Validated and approved listings
rejected_listings     Listings that failed validation with reasons
duplicate_listings    Exact duplicates detected during processing
property_stats        Pipeline statistics and metrics per source


IMPORTANT NOTES

CSV files are only used for local testing
Production system uses MongoDB only
Duplicate listings are stored for tracking only
Pipeline runs daily at 12:00 PM Cairo time
Scrapes from Bayut and OLX, 5 to 10 pages each per run


